{"version":"1","id":"appunite","handle":"appunite","name":"AppUnite","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/81e132ba0ebf4c76a4960b7bec2bed76","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-3.9552,"y":0.5265,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":162,"newest_post_at":"2024-06-27T00:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2021-05-13T12:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.015432,"listicle_ratio":0.074074,"question_ratio":0.216049,"avg_read_time":4.58642,"summary_length_avg":319.875776,"title_length_avg":52.691358,"title_length_var":383.114617,"tag_entropy":4.008933,"tag_diversity":0.574074,"top_tag_share":0.061728,"avg_upvotes":2.58642,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.12963,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.052381,"zero_engagement_share":0.555556,"viral_share":0.006173,"posts_per_week":0.994001,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.117241},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[1.0441,4.4118],"cadence_depth":[1.9706,-3.3824],"hype_variety":[3.5588,7.3235],"title_style":[9.7941,8.9853]},"top_tags":[["general-programming",26],["flutter",18],["mobile",13],["startup",12],["elixir",10],["testing",9],["tech-news",8],["google",8]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Code Review Best Practices","5 common Flutter App issues you might not know but you have in your app","How to increase chances to be hired as a junior frontend developer"],"outlier":["Stop dismissing great ideas because of no software product team! That no longer has to be the case."]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"VTHoakia9","title":"Revolutionizing E-Commerce with AI: The Promise of Virtual Try-On Technology","url":"https://appunite.com/blog/revolutionizing-e-commerce-with-ai","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/revolutionizing-e-commerce-with-ai-the-promise-of-virtual-try-on-technology-vthoakia9","summary":"AI is transforming e-commerce through virtual try-on technology. Featuring the OOTDiffusion framework developed by Xiao-i Research, this technology allows customers to visualize clothing on themselves, enhancing the shopping experience and business efficiency. OOTDiffusion uses outfitting fusion-based latent diffusion techniques and supports multiple platforms for optimal performance. Despite some limitations in accuracy and technological demands, virtual try-on promises significant improvements in customer satisfaction and marketing content generation.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3a9d2cf06d6a0635c677e5ed78eb80f5?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"8ccyjI42G","title":"Reducing the Risk of Technical Change with A/B Testing","url":"https://appunite.com/blog/reducing-the-risk-of-technical-change-with-a-b-testing","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/reducing-the-risk-of-technical-change-with-a-b-testing-8ccyji42g","summary":"Using A/B testing can help mitigate the risks associated with implementing technical changes. In a B2B chat application, an A/B test compared the existing solution for sending attachments with a new implementation using WorkManager. Key metrics such as the success ratio for attachments, the number of attachments sent, and the crash ratio were measured. The results showed significant improvements in the new implementation, leading to a decision to roll out the feature to all users. A/B testing allowed for a data-driven approach to validating the new technical solution without disrupting the user experience.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/0bbda694a306a90c39a91aa9f4cb8225?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"JVHS008su","title":"From Out of memory to Optimus Prime: Fixing a Mobile App Crash for Our Power Users","url":"https://appunite.com/blog/fixing-a-mobile-app-crash-for-our-power-users","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/from-out-of-memory-to-optimus-prime-fixing-a-mobile-app-crash-for-our-power-users-jvhs008su","summary":"This article details how a small development team resolved a critical crash affecting their Android app by analyzing user data and simulating high conversation and blocked user volumes. They implemented measures to prioritize power users and enhance their testing processes.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b3b5178e31cfc86ad915900a84f4c48c?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"RAGN2yNDL","title":"Boosting Login Success Rates: How Analytics Increased User Onboarding by 29%","url":"https://appunite.com/blog/boosting-login-success-rates","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/boosting-login-success-rates-how-analytics-increased-user-onboarding-by-29--ragn2yndl","summary":"A social app increased user onboarding success by 29% through data analysis and addressing key obstacles such as phone verification and deep link issues. This led to a 67% onboarding success rate and an increase in daily active users.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/dc2efef5ed06f63013839591f076d831?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-11T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"IRCVU9dsH","title":"High Velocity Teams: How to Recognize One and Improve Engineering Performance","url":"https://appunite.com/blog/high-velocity-teams-how-to-recognize-one-and-improve-engineering-performance","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/high-velocity-teams-how-to-recognize-one-and-improve-engineering-performance-ircvu9dsh","summary":"Measuring team performance and improving speed, value, and production are key to achieving good performance and delivering valuable work. Teams should focus on doing the work, keeping plans simple, breaking down tasks, delivering small improvements, understanding goals, releasing to production, and making releasing easy. Regularly assessing and discussing these areas with the team can lead to significant improvements.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/306f3580b88212a4507b073c77b331be?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"0Wd44vjWs","title":"4 Signs You're Rushing Your Product Development","url":"https://appunite.com/blog/4-signs-you-re-rushing-your-product-development","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/4-signs-you-re-rushing-your-product-development-0wd44vjws","summary":"Explore four signs that product development was pushed into a feature rush mode, also known as a feature factory. Knowing these signs will allow you to counteract the negative effects to maintain good team morale and the quality of the sprints\u2019 output.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5dbed6325d3377a2baab03f97ec29f66?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"uNrSb93I2","title":"Restructuring for Relevance: Flutter's Future in 2024","url":"https://appunite.com/blog/restructuring-for-relevance-flutter-s-future-in-2024","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/restructuring-for-relevance-flutter-s-future-in-2024-unrsb93i2","summary":"Google recently underwent a restructuring that impacted the Flutter team, but it is not a retreat from Flutter. The development roadmap remains unchanged, and Flutter continues to have a thriving community and ongoing development.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/98fd30eb36fad26eb2687632bb3b60c9?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"fb6Ppq0bD","title":"Flutter WebAssembly (wasm) is finally here!","url":"https://appunite.com/blog/flutter-web-assembly-wasm","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/flutter-webassembly-wasm-is-finally-here--fb6ppq0bd","summary":"Flutter WebAssembly (wasm) support brings significant speed improvements and smoother user experiences to Flutter web applications. WebAssembly can improve performance by up to 2x for frame rendering and 3x for worst-case performance. However, browser support and package compatibility are limitations to consider.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5de4731c6926938f350f44ce0f49471b?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":9,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"v0ccAlPwf","title":"Code coverage for End-to-End tests","url":"https://appunite.com/blog/code-coverage-for-end-to-end-tests","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/code-coverage-for-end-to-end-tests-v0ccalpwf","summary":"Learn how to implement JaCoCo code coverage in Android projects, set up CI/CD for code coverage with GitHub Actions, and integrate Firebase Test Lab for comprehensive testing.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d84265c7a51f25e5f5a688c8abbbd923?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2024-05-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"ToJX3BZko","title":"Google I/O 2024 Keynote: key announcements","url":"https://appunite.com/blog/google-i-o-2024-keynote-announments","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/google-i-o-2024-keynote-key-announcements-tojx3bzko","summary":"Google I/O 2024 Keynote focused on AI-driven innovation and introduced new features like AI Overviews in Google Search, scam detection for Android, Flutter Web with WASM, and Gemini improvements. Project Astra, Project IDX, and Firebase also received updates.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1cc5babc96d62676cd72a087c9954bb2?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-15T00:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["dribbble","oss","swlh","hackernoon","ncameron"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","tbpn","alexfinn","ryolu_","hamelhusain"],"similar":[{"id":"dribbble","handle":"dribbble","name":"Dribbble","is_squad":false,"x":-3.9282,"y":0.4348,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":73,